Although intelligent algorithms have made substantial strides in optimizing Internet of Vehicles (IoV) applications, the pervasive nature of IoV poses significant security and privacy risks. Consequently, novel architectural frameworks are essential to address these challenges and unlock the full potential of IoV. Concurrently, significant academic focus has been drawn towards Federated Learning (FL) and Blockchain as potential solutions for IoV security and privacy concerns. This paper provides a detailed literature survey on integrating FL and Blockchain technologies within IoV environments. Initially, we outline the fundamental concepts, characteristics, and key protocols underlying both FL and Blockchain. Subsequently, we present a comprehensive overview of FL-specific and Blockchain-specific protocols suitable for IoV. Finally, we examine literature that utilizes these technologies individually or in combination to tackle IoV security and privacy issues, simultaneously identifying associated challenges and potential future research directions. To our knowledge, this represents the most extensive survey on Literature - Technology stacks for Security and Privacy - Architecture - Federated Learning - Blockchain implemented within IoV. The necessary groundwork laid out in this paper can guide future research aimed at developing novel approaches to address remaining challenges and maximize the benefits of FL and Blockchain in IoV. Furthermore, this literature review will serve as a valuable resource for selecting appropriate technologies and formulating new solutions to overcome current limitations. Ultimately, this survey will aid in guiding the development of new solutions to surmount existing challenges and fully realize the advantages of FL and Blockchain within IoV. The acronyms and abbreviations used in this survey are detailed in Appendix A (See Table 1), while the taxonomy of this literature survey is illustrated in Figure 1. This work is open access under t